==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leuþą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*lěu-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*lǎu-}}.

Cognate with Old High German {{term|liod|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Lied|lang=de}}), Old Saxon {{term|lioð|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|lied|lang=nl}}), Old Norse {{term|ljóð||verse, song|lang=non}}.

